            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0306" n="1040" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1040"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr.
                            Christiancy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1879</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Gibbs’s No. 300, in
                    reference to the payment of the claims on Peru of Messrs. Sparrow, Noland, Gait,
                    and others, members of the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, I have to
                    inform you that having communicated the substance of that dispatch to the
                    parties interested, or to their representatives, on the 19th and 20th of
                    February last, a letter has been received from Mr. C. G. Lee, attorney for Mr.
                    Sparrow, complaining that the financial agents of Peru in New York, referred to
                    in Mr. Gibbs’s dispatch, have thus far failed to comply with orders given them
                    to make the contemplated payments. Under these circumstances it would seem
                    proper that you bring the matter to the attention of the Peruvian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. M. Evarts.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
